(7233629, 1119621, 138253, '<td valign="top">the orange-purple-green is distracting to me.<br/>i can understand some shadow in the distance, but <strike>the area of purple ground looks to be almost digitally processed into the picture.</strike> <br/>i have since looked up purple sunsets and found that they are becoming more common in areas with a large concentration of air pollution causing the red/yellow/orange waves to be filtered out more, where areas with high concentrations of salt in the air (oceans, etc) have more of the ultraviolet wavelengths filtered out.<br/>revised score on this is getting a 6 from me (and an apology for the implication of digitally ''painting'' or tone-shifting the colors).</td>', 'the orange-purple-green is distracting to me.i can understand some shadow in the distance, but the area of purple ground looks to be almost digitally processed into the picture. i have since looked up purple sunsets and found that they are becoming more common in areas with a large concentration of air pollution causing the red/yellow/orange waves to be filtered out more, where areas with high concentrations of salt in the air (oceans, etc) have more of the ultraviolet wavelengths filtered out.revised score on this is getting a 6 from me (and an apology for the implication of digitally ''painting'' or tone-shifting the colors).', '2014-06-26 16:54:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(7233631, 1119595, 138253, '<td valign="top">deleted silhouette-based comment.<br/> <br/>voting this on it''s own merit without the silhouette challenge as a factor:<br/>i find the row of people on the point to be a fascinating subject to choose to capture, many times over we see a single figure standing triumphantly on a hill in sunset imagery, this is a pleasant break from that norm.<br/>at first i wanted more drama in the sky in the form of some contrasting clouds, but upon just watching this for a while i''m happy with the tranquil scene and the longing for my annual camping trip to the cottage.<br/> <br/>a 6 from me on this</td>', 'deleted silhouette-based comment. voting this on it''s own merit without the silhouette challenge as a factor:i find the row of people on the point to be a fascinating subject to choose to capture, many times over we see a single figure standing triumphantly on a hill in sunset imagery, this is a pleasant break from that norm.at first i wanted more drama in the sky in the form of some contrasting clouds, but upon just watching this for a while i''m happy with the tranquil scene and the longing for my annual camping trip to the cottage. a 6 from me on this', '2014-06-26 16:58:40.000000', NULL, 1),
